@@ -317,6 +317,10 @@ Using the Recommended Project
 
 The Mautic :xref:`Recommended Project` is a template which provides a starter kit for managing your Mautic dependencies with Composer.
 
+.. note::
+
+  By default, the Recommended Project installs Mautic into a ``docroot`` subdirectory of your project. Your web server's document root - or the directory you point your virtual host at - must therefore be set to ``docroot``, not the project root. If you serve the project root directly, Mautic won't be reachable at the expected URL. See :ref:`How can you use another folder than docroot as the root folder?` if you need a different layout.
+
 .. note::
   The instructions below refer to the global Composer installation. You might need to replace Composer with ``php composer.phar`` or something similar for your setup.
 
@@ -344,7 +348,7 @@ What does the Recommended Project template actually do?
 
 When installing the given ``composer.json`` the following occurs:
 
-- Install Mautic in the ``docroot`` directory.
+- Install Mautic in the ``docroot`` directory. This is the directory that must be configured as your web server's document root.
 - Autoloader uses the generated Composer autoloader in ``vendor/autoload.php``, instead of the one provided by Mautic in ``docroot/vendor/autoload.php``.
 - Plugins - packages of type ``mautic-plugin`` - are in ``docroot/plugins/``.
 - Themes - packages of type ``mautic-theme`` - are in ``docroot/themes/``.
